{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>Behold, I am going to die.</b> The inheritance of the land of Israel depends on the birthright, and the inheritance does not come until after four hundred years, as it is written: ״וענו אותם ארבע מאות שנה״ (and they shall afflict them four hundred years). And it is written: ״ודור רביעי ישובו הנה״ (and the fourth generation shall return here). And since I will not live until that time — this is the meaning of 'Behold, I am going to die' — what profit do I have in it, and what do I lose by selling it? <b>And why is this to me, a birthright?</b> If I were to live until that time, so that I myself would inherit it, I would not sell it. Another interpretation: <b>Behold, I am going to die</b> — every day I go to hunt animals in the forests, where bears and lions and wild beasts are found, and I endanger myself to death. And why should I wait for the portion of the birthright that is due to me after my father's death — perhaps I shall die first."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:59.590778860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}